.TH WREX-UDP 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-udp \- udp layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIudp\fR \fB--udp\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIudp\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
UDP (RFC 768): 8\-byte header. length autofilled from header+payload (explicit wins); checksum computed over the RFC 9293 pseudo\-header (src, dst, proto 17, length) plus the segment and payload. Explicit \-\-udp\-checksum=0 produces the scapy\-style unchecked zero.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 30; stacks on ipv4 (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --udp-sport).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-sport=\fIINT\fR\fR
source port Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-dport=\fIINT\fR\fR
destination port Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-length=\fIINT\fR\fR
length incl. header (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-checksum=\fIINT\fR\fR
checksum over pseudo\-header+segment (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \-\-layer ipv4 \-\-layer udp \\\\
  \-\-eth\-dst=ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \\\\
  \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \-\-udp\-sport=4444 \-\-udp\-dport=5555 \\\\
  \-\-payload=hex:deadbeef

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBwrex\fR(1), \fBwrex\-eth\fR(7), \fBwrex\-arp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-ipv4\fR(7), \fBwrex\-icmp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-tcp\fR(7)
